      "message": "That\u0027s not what I think we should test. In fact, the sanitized capabilities must be different in some cases – that\u0027s the point of sanitization.\n\nIf you look at my example snippet, you can see it differs fundamentally on the last line, where it tests that the *UN*sanitized capabilities haven\u0027t been changed.\n\n// The contract for sanitizeCapabilitiesFromAgent requires that it does not mutate\n// its argument. Make sure this is respected.\ntestSanitizedCapabilitiesFromAgentDoesNotMutateArgument() {\n  unsanitized \u003d fill in some NC with everything it can have\n  copyOfUnsanitized \u003d new NC(unsanitized)\n  sanitized \u003d sanitizedCapabilitiesFromAgent\n  assertEquals(copyOfUnsanitized, unsanitized)\n}\n\nBut the returned value certainly should be different, so you could also say :\nassertNotEquals(unsanitized, sanitized)",
